{
  "info": {
    "name": "LJVIS \u2014 Notifications (teavituste moodul)",
    "_postman_id": "ljvis-notifications-v1",
    "description": "Functional tests for the notifications module: in-app notifications (GET /v1/notifications/list, unread-count, POST mark-read, mark-all-read), the Postkast 2.0 outbound send log (outbound-log/list, outbound-log/recipients) and UC-04 resend. Covers the permission boundary (in-app endpoints need auth only and are filtered by the caller's permissions[]; outbound-log/* and resend/* require notification.admin), idempotency (insert_notification ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, mark-read / mark-all-read) and the append-only rule (resend appends a new outbound_log row and never mutates the original). Self-contained: authenticates, seeds notifications + an outbound_log row + recipient via Resql, and exercises the internal notification/create orchestrator. PK 2.0 has no CI mock \u2014 send-postkast returns a mock success (documented TODO in the DSL), so resend is exercised at the HTTP layer. Rust Resql returns camelCase field names; assertions match that.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "[Auth] Login \u2014 Super Admin (has notification.admin)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Login 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "var b = pm.response.json(); var token = typeof b === 'string' ? b : (b.response || b.token || '');",
              "pm.test('JWT received', () => pm.expect(token).to.not.be.empty);",
              "pm.environment.set('cookie_admin', 'customJwtCookie=' + token);"
